the relationship between Hong Kong and  China is at its lowest for decades it  goes back hundreds of years but these  are the six moments you need to  understand to really get why it's become  such an important issue 1842  this is when Britain took control of  part of Hong Kong after the First Opium  War fast-forward five decades and China  gave him the rest of it but only for 99  years 1997 this is when that lease ran  out by that time China had been a  communist state for nearly 50 years and  Hong Kong remained democratic under UK  rule Britain handed control of Hong Kong  back to China who introduced the one  country two systems' rule basically this  meant the Hong Kong would be guaranteed  a high degree of autonomy from China  that would technically still be part of  the country Hong Kong kept a capitalist  economy freedom of speech and a free  press at least until 2047 2003 this was  the first major sign of discontent from  Hong Kong as pro China politicians tried  to introduce a bill that banned  criticizing China it triggered huge  protests with half a million people  taking to the streets the bill was  withdrawn a big win for anti China  protesters 2014 the umbrella movement  went on for months in Hong Kong it was  named that after demonstrators started  using umbrellas to protect themselves  from police teargas  protesters thought China's proposed  changes to Hong Kong's electoral system  were too restrictive thousands protested  and the controversial reforms were  shelved as a result  2019 five years later the biggest  demonstrations yet took place  this time they were triggered by a bill  would make it easier to send people to  mainland China to face trial but the  movement became much bigger and gave  people an opportunity to resist the  growing influence of China in Hong Kong  2047 for many 2047 is the most important  phase this is the year that China is  supposed to get full control of Hong  Kong ending the one country two systems'  rule Chinese leader Xi Jingping recently  changed the law meaning he could be  President for life how he deals at Hong  Kong is going to be a key part of his  presidency he is stuck between not  looking too heavy-handed to the West and  not looking too weak at home whatever  happens is already fraught relationship  isn't showing any signs of improving  [Music]
 

